// os.marco — the OS act surface: the foreign primitives a host fulfills (see
// spec/Hosts.md). Imported by macro programs with `use os.`. Under `--host
// dryrun` these log; under `--host windows` they perform real input; under
// `--host bridge:<exe>` an external program (e.g. AHK) performs them.

the OS is an act.
this exports Key.       // press a named key, e.g. "e" or "enter"
this exports KeyDown.    // press and HOLD a key (released by a later KeyUp)
this exports KeyUp.      // release a held key
this exports Type.      // type a text string
this exports Click.     // click; input may be a Point to move-then-click
this exports Move.      // move the cursor to a Point
this exports Sleep.     // sleep N milliseconds (a number)
this exports Color.     // read the pixel at a Point; result is a hex text
this exports Focus.     // ok if the active window matches the given text
this exports Repeat.    // press a key on an interval until the frame is canceled
this exports Spam.      // start the background spam loop: { Key|Button, Every }
this exports StopSpam.  // stop the background spam loop
this exports Roll.      // random number in [Min, Max]; result is the number
this exports EightBall. // random Magic 8-Ball answer; result is the text
this exports Name.      // random fantasy name; result is the text
this exports Find.      // resolve an Anchor (Image match, else Colour at X,Y) -> Point
this exports Secret.    // type a stored secret by name (value never in the route)
this exports Activate.  // focus a named app, launching it if not running (e.g. "chrome")
this exports Launch.    // start an app/path/URL via the shell (e.g. "steam://rungameid/...")
this exports Restore.   // return focus to the window that was in front before the last Activate

// A screen coordinate, passed to Click / Move / Color.
the Point is a set.
this's X is a number.
this's Y is a number.
